Z||000000||beachbomb||12-03-2000||10:57 AM||||I got my second Indy yesterday! Special thanks to Joel(turbo86se) for finding it and letting me know about it. Went to Mrytle Beach S.C. to get it, has alot of rust on frame but this will be my "parts Indy" for my primary Indy. All Indy specific things are in excellent shape and interior is near mint. thanks again to Joel!!!..Jim(2 '84 Indy's) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||2xsess||12-03-2000||11:37 AM||||Sweet <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>You should have let me know you were heading up this way, me and Steve could have met you somewhere and checked it out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>Post some pics if you can. <BR>Good Luck <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||12-03-2000||12:27 PM||||You're welcome Jim!! I just wished I could have been there when you hauled it away! I should start a Fiero-locator service, a few months ago I found a sweet 87GT for sale for a guy in NC for a low price! <BR>How did the decklid turn out for you? Did you take lots of pictures? I'd really like to see them!! I'm glad you got the Fiero, and hopefully I'll be able to check it out when I'm down there again. Isn't there another meeting soon?  <P>I just remembered seeing another Indy in Latta, SC. Interested?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||beachbomb||12-03-2000||05:48 PM||||Hey Joel, how much!!! Honestly i don't think my wife would let me cram another Indy in the garage!! Maybe i could hide it some-where!?!?! oh well, thanks again Joel..Jim<BR>p.s. Sorry Jeff, i totally forgot about you being in Ga.!||||reg||12
Z||000004||FieroMaster88||12-03-2000||08:41 PM||||Ok, you guys seem to know about indy's, how about giving me some advice?  I have an 84 Indy Fiero.  It is in rough shape, well, at least the interior is.  All the leather needs to be re-wraped, the red parts on the seats have cigarette burns, the dash is cracked all over the place, the steering column has about 6" of play in any direction and the back window is blown out!  The body needs cleaning (big time) and the front facia is cracked.<P>The good parts are that the frame is solid and that the car runs like new.  I need to decide what to do with it.  If I am gonna restore it, i will need to find some Interior parts for a good deal, or should I just sell it for scrap.  Please give me an Idea of what to do!?!?!?!<P>Thanks,<P>James||||reg||1
Z||000005||beachbomb||12-04-2000||04:34 PM||||HOW MUCH!!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. Honestly, Indy parts are insanely hard to find, hence the reason i bought another Indy, basically for a parts car for my primary Indy. You'll never find an Indy in the bone-yard, rarely do you see Indy parts on ebay, and when you do, you pay out the a*s!!!. if you really want to keep it just keep looking in local car trader magazines(thats how i found my good Indy), the internet and anywhere else you can look for used cars. Where are you located? If you do decide to "scrap" it(it hurts me to say that word) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> let me know before hand, i may want it! If you have and questions about it please e-mail me. I bought my first Indy in april and have only found a few Indy's for sale since, try talking to the "fiero factory" website, i beleive he has 5 Indys parts cars on hand at this time, hes in Alabama....plmk, thanks..Jim||||reg||14
